>> title: Buttermilk Pancakes
>> servings: 4
>> time: 25 minutes
>> tags: familiar, watchme, breakfast, griddle, timing-sensitive

Whisk @all-purpose flour{1.5%cups}, @sugar{2%tbsp}, @baking powder{2%tsp}, @baking soda{1/2%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} in a #mixing bowl{}.

Whisk @buttermilk{1.25%cups}, @egg{1}, and @melted butter{3%tbsp} in another #bowl{}.

Fold wet ingredients into dry ingredients until just combined; leave small lumps and rest for ~{5%minutes}.

-- watch: Griddle is hot enough that a water drop dances and evaporates quickly.
Heat a #griddle{} over medium heat and brush with @neutral oil{1%tsp}.

-- watch: Pancake tops show many popped bubbles and edges look dry.
Pour @batter{1/4%cup} per pancake and cook until bubbles appear, about ~{2%minutes}.

-- watch: Underside is golden brown, not pale or dark.
Flip with a #spatula{} and cook the second side for ~{1%minute}.

Serve with @maple syrup{} and @butter{}.
